[x] 66 Shift Register node -- and the multi-output ports it needs. One input,
       N outputs (2..16, "outputs" property). Every arriving message is stored
       at the head of an open-ended shift register: message k leaves on
       output 1, message k-1 on output 2, ... message k-N+1 on output N; the
       oldest falls off the end. Stages not yet filled stay silent. Emission
       order is oldest stage first, output 1 last, so a downstream multi-input
       node triggered from output 1 already sees the other stages updated.
       This settles the port-model question #56 left open: multi-output is
       the mirror image of multi-input.
